Z||000003||terryk||12-27-2000||08:58 PM||||Start wandering the wreckers for an 84 SE. These have the glass sail panels vs the 85 and up plastic. They will bolt right in. Take:<P>1. 10mm and 11mm socket with 1/4" drive.<BR>2. Flat blade screw driver<BR>3. large Philips screw driver<BR>4. Needle nose pliers. <BR>5. T45 Torx with 3/8" drive and ratchet.<BR>6. Optionally, the Jaws-of-Life...<P>Where to use them will be revealed when you start to take them out. <P>Get the two clips on the body. You will wish you had if you don't.<P>When you install them you will find that the plastic panels are about a 1/4" longer on the diagonal edge than the glass. They will have worn the paint off and the glass panels won't quite cover it. You can use touch up paint or a black plastic strip to cover it up.<P>...but no more cracking panels. ||||reg||1
